From 28e62940ecdcc651357fe822018bf3fa5c099d85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Casaroli <marco.casaroli@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:47:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fs: Truncate on open with O_RDWR and O_TRUNC.

Commit 9e141acab36 changed O_RDWR to 2, so O_RDWR no longer contains
the O_WRONLY bit.  tmpfs, FAT, SmartFS and NFS still test
(oflags & (O_TRUNC | O_WRONLY)) == (O_TRUNC | O_WRONLY) in open.  This
test is false for O_RDWR: open(O_RDWR | O_TRUNC) and fopen("w+") keep
the old contents of the file.

Test the access mode with O_ACCMODE, as mnemofs does.  O_TRUNC without
write access is still ignored.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Marco Casaroli <marco.casaroli@gmail.com>
---
 fs/fat/fs_fat32.c          | 2 +-
 fs/nfs/nfs_vfsops.c        | 2 +-
 fs/smartfs/smartfs_smart.c | 2 +-
 fs/tmpfs/fs_tmpfs.c        | 2 +-
 4 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/fat/fs_fat32.c b/fs/fat/fs_fat32.c
index d5199d5b5a054..2eed2411f17c9 100644
--- a/fs/fat/fs_fat32.c
+++ b/fs/fat/fs_fat32.c
@@ -534,7 +534,7 @@ static int fat_open(FAR struct file *filep, FAR const char *relpath,
        * access is ignored.
        */
 
-      if ((oflags & (O_TRUNC | O_WRONLY)) == (O_TRUNC | O_WRONLY))
+      if ((oflags & O_TRUNC) != 0 && (oflags & O_ACCMODE) != O_RDONLY)
         {
           /* Truncate the file to zero length.  If the file is already
            * open elsewhere, the shared state is updated as well so that
